# Git branch workflow

- **Default branch:** Do day-to-day work on **`dev`**. Prefer staying on `dev` unless a task explicitly requires another branch.
- **When pushing changes:** Do not push straight to `main` as the first step.
  1. Commit on **`dev`** (while checked out on `dev`).
  2. **`git push origin dev`**
  3. Merge **`dev` → `main`** (e.g. `git checkout main`, `git merge dev`, `git push origin main`, or an equivalent PR merge on the host).
  4. **`git checkout dev`** so the working copy is back on **`dev`**.

After any merge or push workflow that touched `main`, end on **`dev`** unless the user asked otherwise.
